  "contract": {
    "transaction": "SlotTransactions remembers the original Invocation state identity while Graph owns a cohort. Foreign take/take_all/recover reject before mutation. Moving the original Invocation and legal later rebind remain supported. Identity is borrowed while state lives, not resource permission.",
    "stage": "GLM/DeepSeek project existing immutable phase input IDs into the original live lease table using a static borrowed range. Eager bounds check precedes any Graph bind. Same execute body, no argument vector or extra ReadLease pin.",
    "phase": "Existing cold split already proves producer/availability. Routed expert selection and bounded upload require the original host phase boundary; do not add a parallel plan or erase that boundary.",
    "lifetime": "Original live/completed outputs, resident expert-bank generation, Invocation, Completion, reset, Status, publication and actual retirement remain at their original release points.",
    "allocation": "StoreSource tickets/coordinates inline up to2 with original allocator overflow; native paged instructions inline up to4. Retained group words reserve before revoke/upload and commit trivial content after upload. All original actual permission/layout/coordinate checks remain.",
    "memory": "No new GPU buffer. Inline owner allocation is charged with actual sizeof; removes small child allocations but may increase single-view metadata bytes. No claim of lower total metadata or VRAM."
  },
